sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SV as Calling service (e.g. StudentDataService)
    participant G as AccessGuardService
    participant K as AttributeKeyService
    participant E as IDataEncryptor
    participant R as IGenericRepository
    participant DB as SQL Server
    SV->>G: CheckAccessAsync(accessorId, studentId, dataAttributeIds, consentPurposeId or null)
    G->>R: Accessor's roles, active policies, student's granted unexpired consents, active purposes and their attributes
    R->>DB: SELECT
    DB-->>R: rows
    G->>G: Allow attributes covered by a consent under a purpose the roles have an active policy for
    opt some attributes still refused
        G->>R: Approved, unexpired emergency access of the accessor for this student
        G->>G: Allow every attribute (no purpose)
    end
    G-->>SV: List of AccessDecision (isAllowed, consentPurposeId, isEmergencyAccess)
    SV->>K: DecryptValuesAsync(allowed values only)
    K->>R: Load attribute keys
    K->>E: Unwrap data key (HKDF-derived wrapping key of the key's master version), then AES-256-GCM decrypt bound to row and field
    E-->>K: plaintext, or erased when the key was destroyed
    K-->>SV: AttributeValue list
    SV->>G: LogAccessBatchAsync(accessorId, entries)
    G->>R: PrepareCreate one ACCESSLOGS row per value shown, SaveAsync()
    R->>DB: INSERT ACCESSLOGS
    Note over SV: Refused attributes are returned as "exists, not shared", never with a value
